  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CoE Countering Economic Crime in Serbia</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">CoE Mot ekonomisk brottslighet</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Den f&#xf6;reslagna insatsen avser forts&#xe4;ttningen av det p&#xe5;g&#xe5;ende programmet &quot;Preventing Money Laundering and Terrorist Financing in Serbia&quot;, som Sverige har st&#xf6;tt sedan januari 2020. Programmet genomf&#xf6;rs av Europar&#xe5;det (CoE).

Det &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;let &#xe4;r att st&#xe4;rka huvudpelarna i AML/CFT-f&#xf6;rebyggande och verkst&#xe4;llighetsregimen i Serbien och uppdatera dess policy i linje med de nya europeiska och internationella standarderna, genom att fokusera p&#xe5;:

1. F&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra mekanismer f&#xf6;r att f&#xf6;rebygga ML/FT som till&#xe4;mpas av de serbiska myndigheterna, tillsynsorganen och den privata sektorn, i linje med identifierade risker och nya hot,

2. F&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrad juridisk och operativ kapacitet f&#xf6;r uppt&#xe4;ckt, utredning och sanktionering av ML och TF och

3. System f&#xf6;r &#xe5;tervinning och f&#xf6;rvaltning av tillg&#xe5;ngar optimerade f&#xf6;r att s&#xe4;kerst&#xe4;lla snabb identifiering och sp&#xe5;rning av olagliga int&#xe4;kter och effektivt bortskaffande av beslagtagna och konfiskerade tillg&#xe5;ngar.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The contribution concerns the continuation of the ongoing program &quot;Preventing Money Laundering and Terrorist Financing in Serbia&quot;, which Sweden has supported since January 2020. The program is implemented by the CoE.

The overall objective is to strengthen the main pillars of AML/CFT prevention and enforcement regime in Serbia and update its policies in line with the new European and international standards, by focusing on:

1. Enhancing mechanisms for the prevention of ML/FT that are applied by the Serbian authorities, supervisory bodies and private sector, in line with identified risks and emerging threats,

2. Improved legal and operational capacities for detection, investigation and sanctioning of ML and TF and

3. Asset recovery and asset management systems optimized to ensure swift identification and tracing of illicit proceeds and effective disposal of seized and confiscated assets.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the intervention is to strengthen the main pillars of AML/CTF prevention and enforcement regime in Serbia and update its policies in line with the new European and international standards (revised recommendations of the Financial Action Task Force, 6th Anti-Money Laundering Directive and the new EU Anti-Money Laundering Regulation). The overall objective is broken down into 3 outcomes, as follows:

Outcome 1: Enhanced mechanisms for prevention of economic crimes, including corruption and ML/TF, applied by the Serbian authorities and private sector, in line with identified risks and emerging threats;

Outcome 2: Improved legal and operational capacities for detection, investigation and sanctioning of corruption, money laundering and terrorism financing and

Outcome 3: Asset recovery and asset management systems optimized to ensure swift identification, tracing of illicit proceeds and effective confiscation and disposal of seized and confiscated assets.</narrative>
  </description>
